# Custom local app URL handlers (optional; supplements auto-discovered desktop apps & web apps).
# Format: Label|||pattern|||command
#   Label   : name shown in the picker and referenced by rules.conf
#   pattern : boundary-aware plain text, glob */?, or regex:RE (Python regex syntax)
#   command : how to open matching URLs:
#               - direct argv command (no outer shell); use {url} where the URL goes (if omitted,
#                 appended last). Do not place {url} inside a `sh -c '...'` script string — pass
#                 it as a positional argument instead (e.g. `sh -c 'mycmd "$1"' _ {url}`).
#               - "uri:<template>" rewrites the URL to a non-http(s) URI scheme and dispatches to
#                 its installed XDG handler; placeholders: {url}, {host}, {path}, {path_no_slash},
#                 {query}, {query_part}, {fragment}, {fragment_part}, and {1}..{9} for regex groups
#               - "disabled" hides an auto-discovered app with the same Label (use "*" for always)
#
# Built-in auto-discovered desktop apps (when installed):
#   T3 Code, Spotify, Zoom, Slack, Telegram, Discord, Linear, Notion, Figma, Steam, Signal, Matrix
# Installed Omarchy/Chromium web apps (.desktop files) are also auto-discovered.
#
# Examples (commented out):
# Element — Web App|||app.element.io|||omarchy-launch-webapp {url} --profile-directory="Profile 3"
# Basecamp — Web App|||3.basecamp.com|||omarchy-launch-webapp {url} --profile-directory="Profile 3"
# My Local App|||regex:^https://app\.example\.com/items/([^/?#]+)|||uri:myapp://item/{1}
# GitHub — Web App|||*|||disabled
